{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the alafim.</b> The oxen that plow — like them, and likewise the ayarim, as in 'the young of your alafim' (Deuteronomy 7:13):" "<b>Belil.</b> As in 'whether the ox labors upon his belil' (Job 6:5):" "<b>Chamitz.</b> Also chametz are equivalent:" "<b>Asher zaroh.</b> It:" "<b>Rachat.</b> From the root of ruach, and it is an instrument, and in the winnowing fork:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:05.527446189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}